{title: Be Thou My Vision}
{artist: Irish, c. 8th cent.; tr. Mary E. Byrne (1905), versified Eleanor H. Hull (1912)}
{key: D}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 3/4}
{meta: tune SLANE - Traditional Irish melody (1909)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1912, tune 1909: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Be Thou my [G]Vision, O [D]Lord of my heart;
[G]Naught be all [D]else to me, [Em]save that Thou [A]art;
[Bm]Thou my best [A]thought, by [G]day or by [D]night,
[G]Waking or [D]sleeping, Thy [A]presence my [D]light.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Be Thou my [G]Wisdom, and [D]Thou my true Word;
[G]I ever [D]with Thee and [Em]Thou with me, [A]Lord;
[Bm]Thou my great [A]Father, [G]I Thy true [D]son;
[G]Thou in me [D]dwelling, and [A]I with Thee [D]one.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Riches I [G]heed not, nor [D]man's empty praise,
[G]Thou mine in[D]heritance, [Em]now and al[A]ways:
[Bm]Thou and Thou [A]only, [G]first in my [D]heart,
[G]High King of [D]Heaven, my [A]Treasure Thou [D]art.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]High King of [G]Heaven, my [D]victory won,
[G]May I reach [D]Heaven's joys, O [Em]bright Heaven's [A]Sun!
[Bm]Heart of my [A]own heart, what[G]ever be[D]fall,
[G]Still be my [D]Vision, O [A]Ruler of [D]all.
{end_of_verse}
